  "_approach": "The kick-removal break: bars 1-2 run the full uplifting groove, then the kick vanishes for bars 3-4 while the offbeat open hat, closed 16th hat and a rising tambourine/shaker layer keep the pulse alive on their own — Native Instruments' UK garage/garage-adjacent 'remove and reintroduce the groove' technique applied to a trance breakdown-to-build transition. The kick punches back in on the very last 16th to pick the track back up into the drop. (re-voiced for the Vermona DRM1 MKIII's 8 channels)",
